# Tracer: AbsProduct with evaluated closed rational factors.
# Before: these direct goals missed the literal abs(a)*abs(b) matcher.
# forall x R:
#     abs(2*x)=2*abs(x)
# Now: the same absolute-value law evaluates symbol-free rational factors.
# Boundary: symbolic factors need their absolute value; wrong signs and WD fail.
# Gate: target/release/litex -lang en -strict -f examples/proof_nodes/equal/by_builtin_rule/abs_product_closed_coefficient.lit
forall x R:
    abs(2*x)=2*abs(x)
    abs(-3*x)=3*abs(x)
    abs(x*(-3/2))=(3/2)*abs(x)
    abs((1+1)*x)=2*abs(x)
    abs(2*x)=(1+1)*abs(x)
    abs(x*2)=abs(x)*2

forall f fn(t R) R, x R:
    abs(-3*f(x))=3*abs(f(x))
